    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="1055" n="945" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg945"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.6712A/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-19T21:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 19,
                                1928—9 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Department’s 37, April 13, 6 p.m. The Department today handed Turkish
                    Ambassador drafts of proposed treaties of arbitration and of conciliation. The
                    texts of the proposed treaties will be forwarded in the next pouch.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d776-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d776-f1" n="11" xml:id="d776-f1-content">
                <p>Draft treaties not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
